                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "9/2/2019\nLooks like where the game is now is where it shall remain based off a discussion with LInsoDeTeh. He did fix one last bug I reported but development is considered finished. \n\n\n2017 Review \n\nIf you enjoy sand box games, creativity, or working mechanics to produce a result.. you will find many lost hours here. \n\nI won't lie, this game was a little confusing at first which left me not really wanting to play. I watched the video tutorials by the developer, checked out the wiki, and searched the web and steam forums but still found myself lacking in much information. The things I questioned, the developer happily not only answered but explained in details. I decided to compile a [url=http://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=870732972]guide[/url] with information to help newcomers get started a lot quicker than me. As well as included details about the achievements. \n\nOnce I got the hang of things I quickly became consumed by accumulating the whole world, building automated systems  and producing as many resources and cash as I could to level my world. And mind you, the world feels endless so far. I really enjoy that you can basically collect almost everything you destroy, minus resources that require building a Mining Tower to collect. \n\nI forgot to mention this when I initially wrote my review, one major positive for me is that you can construct your things in any of the materials/textures you collect. I love having that kind of variety. \n\nThere are \"ship yards\" in the open world to salvage random pieces and parts. Four AI factions with different resources and plans to collect and learn. As i have explored my world while i encounter some buildings from the same factions, they don't look exactly the same, but are made of the same materials so I can gather them if needed for reproducing in the Research Lab. \n\nThe missions seem pretty cool. Scattered through the world at notable looking structures. Giving you something more to do besides harvesting everything. I have not had the pleasure of PVE team missions or PVP arena as I haven't found anyone to play with. So you guys should pick it up and holler :D: \n\nThe only real negative mark for me is that even with running a decent system (specs below), I get a lot of delays. Not enough to deter me, but sometimes it does give me PMS and sometimes it just straight up crashes and exits. \nMost notably if i pan to my base too quickly without a hesitation the game exits. Probably cause of all the stuff I have going on there. \nAlso has seemed like, the more i have built, the more i have automated, the more ships i have gathering crystal resources, the bigger the delay is when i manually click on blocks to collect them with my ship in range to loot. I can click out a whole asteroid with no delays if my ship is not in range, but then there is a large delay when I bring the ship in to auto \"vacuum\" up the blocks. I suspect its the game waiting to catch up with what just happened. \n\n\nSystem: \nMobo: Asus x99 Deluxe \nCPU: i7 5820K\nGPU: duel GTX 970 EVGA Superclocked\nRAM: 16x Corsair Vengeance LPX\nHDD: 4TB WD Black + 1TB WD Black\nMonitors: one 27\" + two 23\" LED, 2ms\nKeyboard: G910 Orion Spark \nMouse: Trackball (Kensington Orbit)\nOS: Win 10\n\nAll in all I recommend this game if you are into this genre. \nIf you are looking for quick achievements this is not for you.",
